+# Demo 3: signed UKI update from the laptop registry
+
+Expect 6 to 40 seconds.
+
+A UKI is a bootable unified kernel image.
+
+This procedure serves version 3 from the laptop, stages it with `updatectl`, and boots it.
+
+Complete [Demo 1](demo-flash.md) before this procedure.
+
+Do not call `make demo-update` or `scripts/3-demo-update.py`.
+
+Follow the common requirements in [README.md](README.md).
+
+Once the registry starts, always complete stage 5 before the final report.
+
+If an earlier stage fails, stop both jobs and report the original error.
+
+## 1. Start the laptop registry
+
+Make sure that `output/k3-uefi/registry/SHA256SUMS` exists.
+
+Start this command as a managed background job from `buildroot`.
+
+```sh
+python3 - <<'PY'
+import functools
+import http.server
+import socket
+
+class IPv6Server(http.server.ThreadingHTTPServer):
+    address_family = socket.AF_INET6
+
+handler = functools.partial(http.server.SimpleHTTPRequestHandler, directory="output/k3-uefi/registry")
+IPv6Server(("::", 8000), handler).serve_forever()
+PY
+```
+
+Record the registry job ID.
+
+Tell the user that the registry listens on `[::]:8000`.
+
+## 2. Connect the board to the registry
+
+Start this SSH command as a second managed background job from `buildroot`.
+
+```sh
+ssh -6 -N \
+  -o ExitOnForwardFailure=yes \
+  -o BatchMode=yes \
+  -o ConnectTimeout=10 \
+  -o IdentitiesOnly=yes \
+  -o StrictHostKeyChecking=no \
+  -i output/k3-uefi/build/k3-keys/root_ed25519 \
+  -R '[::1]:8000:[::1]:8000' \
+  root@fe80::b28c:b3ff:fe9a:79a8%wlp0s20f3
+```
+
+Record the tunnel job ID.
+
+Wait up to ten seconds for this board command to return the checksum document.
+
+```sh
+wget -q -O- http://[::1]:8000/SHA256SUMS
+```
+
+If the tunnel fails, report its complete background job output.
+
+In that case, stop the registry job.
+
+Then stop.
+
+Tell the user that the board reaches the laptop registry through loopback.
+
+## 3. Record and stage the update
+
+1. Operate `updatectl list --no-pager` over SSH.
+2. Show the result.
+3. Operate `grep IMAGE_VERSION /usr/lib/os-release` over SSH.
+4. Show the result.
+5. Remove stale version 3 UKIs with this board command.
+
+```sh
+rm -f /boot/EFI/Linux/rva23_3.efi /boot/EFI/Linux/rva23-recovery_3.efi /boot/EFI/Linux/rva23-debug_3.efi
+```
+
+6. Operate `ls /boot/EFI/Linux` over SSH.
+7. Show the remaining UKIs.
+8. Operate `updatectl update host` over SSH with a 1200-second timeout.
+9. Make sure that the command stages version 3 without a signature error.
+10. Operate `updatectl list --no-pager` over SSH.
+11. Show version 3.
+12. Read the registry background output.
+13. Show one artifact request to the user.
+
+Tell the user which version ran before the update and which version is staged.
+
+## 4. Boot version 3
+
+1. Operate `bootctl set-default rva23_3.efi` over SSH.
+2. Operate `systemctl reboot >/dev/null 2>&1 < /dev/null &` over SSH.
+3. Expect the board to reboot even when SSH returns an error.
+4. Wait five seconds.
+5. Wait up to 300 seconds for SSH to answer again.
+6. Operate `grep IMAGE_VERSION /usr/lib/os-release` over SSH.
+7. Make sure that the result contains `IMAGE_VERSION="3"`.
+8. Operate `updatectl list --no-pager` over SSH.
+9. Make sure that the host target shows version 3.
+10. Operate `systemd-sysext status --no-pager` over SSH.
+11. Make sure that version 3 graphics, k3s, and Podman extensions appear under `/usr`.
+
+## 5. Clean up and report
+
+1. When the tunnel background job remains active, stop it.
+2. Stop the registry background job.
+3. Collect both job results.
+4. Report any unexpected error.
+5. Tell the user that version 3 boots from the laptop-delivered UKI.
+
+Do not leave the registry or tunnel running for later demos.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- The board downloads the signed artifacts through the reverse tunnel.
+- `updatectl update host` stages version 3.
+- `bootctl` selects `rva23_3.efi`.
+- The rebooted system reports `IMAGE_VERSION="3"`.
+- The version 3 graphics, k3s, and Podman extensions merge under `/usr`.
+- Both background jobs stop before the final report.
