+# Demo 2: black screen to a graphical desktop
+
+Expect 20 to 25 seconds for the talk demonstration.
+
+KVM devices control the board and capture video.
+
+A system extension adds signed files to `/usr`.
+
+This procedure enables Weston and tests both panel launchers with keyboard, mouse, and screenshots.
+
+Do not call `make demo-weston` or `scripts/2-demo-weston.py`.
+
+Follow the common requirements in [README.md](README.md).
+
+## 1. Discover the video and input devices
+
+1. Call `kvm.getVideoCaptureDevices`.
+2. Select the K3 video path.
+3. Call `kvm.getInputDevices`.
+4. Select the K3 input path.
+5. Tell the user which video and input paths you will use.
+
+Save screenshots under `output/demo/screenshots` with this command from `buildroot`.
+
+Replace `<selected-video-path>` with the stage 1 video path.
+
+Replace `NAME` with a descriptive filename.
+
+```sh
+DEMO_KVM_DEVICE='<selected-video-path>' python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path; import sys; sys.path.insert(0, "scripts"); import demo_lib; print(demo_lib.screenshot(Path("output/demo/screenshots/NAME.jpg")))'
+```
+
+Read each saved image with `read_image`.
+
+Show each saved image inline with an absolute Markdown image link.
+
+## 2. Show the console without Weston
+
+1. Operate `systemctl stop weston.service 2>/dev/null || true` over SSH.
+2. Operate `rm -rf /var/lib/weston` over SSH.
+3. Wait up to ten seconds until `systemctl is-active weston.service` stops returning `active`.
+4. If Weston remains active, report `FAIL`.
+5. In that case, stop.
+6. Save `weston-black.jpg`.
+7. Show the saved image inline.
+8. Make sure that the image shows a console or blank screen without a desktop.
+
+Tell the user that the desktop is absent.
+
+## 3. Enable Weston and merge the signed extension
+
+1. Operate `mkdir -p /var/lib/weston` over SSH.
+2. Operate `touch /var/lib/weston/enabled` over SSH.
+3. Operate `cat /etc/systemd/system/weston-autostart.path` over SSH.
+4. Wait up to twenty seconds for `weston.service` to become active.
+5. If the path unit does not start Weston, operate `systemctl start weston.service`.
+6. Make sure that `systemctl is-active weston.service` returns `active`.
+7. Operate `systemd-sysext --image-policy=root=signed+absent:usr=signed+absent refresh` over SSH.
+8. Make sure that the signed refresh succeeds.
+9. Operate `systemd-sysext status --no-pager` over SSH.
+10. Make sure that the `/usr` hierarchy includes a `graphics_` extension.
+11. Operate `command -v weston-terminal` over SSH.
+12. Make sure that the result is `/usr/bin/weston-terminal`.
+13. Operate `command -v es2gears_wayland` over SSH.
+14. Make sure that the result is `/usr/bin/es2gears_wayland`.
+15. Operate `ls -la /run/weston` over SSH.
+16. Make sure that `wayland-1` appears.
+17. Save `weston-desktop.jpg`.
+18. Show the saved image inline.
+19. Make sure that the desktop and both top-left launcher icons are visible.
+
+Tell the user that the signed graphics extension supplies both launcher programs.
+
+## 4. Test the terminal launcher
+
+1. Read the terminal icon position from the latest screenshot.
+2. Use normalized KVM coordinates from zero through 4096.
+3. Use approximately `x=42` and `y=60` for the leftmost icon at 1920 by 1080.
+4. Call `kvm.sendMouseInput` with `doubleClick`, the left button, and the terminal coordinates.
+5. Wait two seconds.
+6. Save `weston-terminal.jpg`.
+7. Make sure that a terminal window is visible.
+8. If no terminal appears, operate `journalctl -u weston.service -n 30 --no-pager` before one retry.
+9. Call `kvm.pressKeys` with W3C key codes to type `echo TERMINAL_OK`.
+10. Press `Enter` with `kvm.pressKeys`.
+11. Wait one second.
+12. Save `weston-terminal-test.jpg`.
+13. Make sure that the visible terminal output contains `TERMINAL_OK`.
+14. Operate `ps | grep '[w]eston-terminal'` over SSH.
+15. Make sure that a terminal process appears.
+
+Show the terminal test screenshot inline.
+
+Report the visible result.
+
+## 5. Test the graphics launcher
+
+1. Read the gears icon position from the latest desktop screenshot.
+2. Use approximately `x=112` and `y=60` for the second icon at 1920 by 1080.
+3. Call `kvm.sendMouseInput` with `doubleClick`, the left button, and the gears coordinates.
+4. Wait three seconds.
+5. Save `weston-gears.jpg`.
+6. Make sure that the animated gears window is visible.
+7. Operate `ps | grep '[e]s2gears_wayland'` over SSH.
+8. Make sure that an `es2gears_wayland` process appears.
+9. If the process is absent, operate `journalctl -u weston.service -n 30 --no-pager` before one retry.
+10. When the process exists but the window is blank or missing, report `FAIL`.
+
+Show the gears screenshot inline.
+
+A panel double click can open two gears windows.
+
+Make sure that every visible gears window renders.
+
+Call `present` with these files.
+
+- `buildroot/output/demo/screenshots/weston-desktop.jpg`
+- `buildroot/output/demo/screenshots/weston-terminal-test.jpg`
+- `buildroot/output/demo/screenshots/weston-gears.jpg`
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- Weston changes from inactive to active after the enable file appears.
+- `systemd-sysext status` shows a merged graphics extension.
+- The terminal opens from its panel icon.
+- The terminal shows the typed `TERMINAL_OK` result.
+- The gears open from their panel icon and render visibly.
+- The user receives inline screenshots and three presented screenshot files.

